%% CoreLink — DSR erasure flow (LGPD Art. 18 / GDPR Art. 17)
%% Source of truth: specs/03_architecture/privacy_model.md §6, §8,
%%                  crate corelink-privacy-erasure-worker,
%%                  crate corelink-erasure-attestation.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Sub as Data subject
    participant Tn as Tenant admin
    participant UI as Admin UI / DSR API
    participant DPA as DPA + identity proof
    participant DQ as DSR queue (DO)
    participant EW as Erasure worker
    participant R as R2 (cas/ac/audit)
    participant N as Neon (account meta)
    participant Att as Attestation signer

    Sub->>Tn: erasure request (LGPD/GDPR right)
    Tn->>UI: submit DSR ticket (subject scope, evidence)
    UI->>DPA: verify identity + lawful basis
    DPA-->>UI: verified
    UI->>DQ: enqueue (ticket_id, SLA 30d EU / 15d BR)
    DQ->>EW: dispatch
    EW->>R: locate refs (tenant_id, digests, audit pointers)
    EW->>R: tombstone CAS objects (no overwrite-in-place, refcount=0)
    EW->>R: redact AC entries pointing to subject digests
    EW->>N: pseudonymize / drop account row (per retention §8)
    Note over R: Audit log entries are NOT erased<br/>(immutability invariant); subject IDs<br/>pseudonymized in-place per privacy_model §8
    EW->>Att: request signed attestation (Ed25519)
    Att-->>EW: attestation cert + Merkle inclusion proof
    EW->>DQ: mark complete + persist attestation
    UI-->>Tn: notify (signed PDF + JSON receipt)
    Tn-->>Sub: deliver attestation
